From 838490a6fd7f0a026f3c03b2586d0e9f4288a968 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hank Yeomans <hank@quorra.ah.local>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 00:03:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 15/51] sm120 page-split: never free buffers captured by CUDA
 graphs; pre-size from pool geometry

E23 R1 bug B (DSpark K=2 graph mode: cudaErrorIllegalAddress / Xid 31 in the
first attention layer on the second request, eager never faults).

Root cause: _split_kv_pages_to_64 kept its page mask and split-output buffers
in get_resources().buffers as grow-only tensors and *freed* the old tensor on
growth. The warmup only touches the SWA pool (mask N=71), CUDA graphs are
captured with that pointer baked into the memset, _page_mark_kernel and
_page_split_kernel launches, and the first real prefill after capture grows the
shared mask (N=1206) and the "extra" split buffer for the compressed pools.
Every replay then wrote the freed block: silent corruption of whatever the
caching allocator placed there (run H: verify positions/out_cache_loc read back
as int8 page marks, 0x00010100), and an MMU fault once the segment was released.

Fix:
- _grow_persistent retires the old tensor into buffers["flash_mla_sm120_retired"]
  instead of dropping it, so a captured graph stays self-consistent with the
  buffer it captured (a pool's page count never changes after init). A grow
  after capture now logs at ERROR.
- reserve_split_buffers(pools, device) pre-sizes mask and split buffers from
  the maximum over all pools; DeepseekV4AttnBackend calls it at init on SM120
  with (num_pages, page_size, tag) from the SWA and compressed pools, keyed on
  the pool tensors' indexed device (torch.device("cuda") vs "cuda:0" stringify
  differently -- the first attempt reserved under the wrong key).
- _page_mark_kernel takes an N_tok upper bound and drops indices outside
  [0, N_tok) (defense in depth; FlashInfer's SM120 kernel has no upper-bound
  check on positive indices).

Diagnostics kept behind env flags (off by default):
- SGLANG_SM120_IDX_GUARD=1: mask out-of-range token indices to -1 and record
  in-graph OOB stats (idx_oob_stats_buffer, int64[5]).
- SGLANG_BCG_DEBUG_LAYER_BREAKS=all|"0-9"|"0,4": per-layer graph breaks for
  fault attribution; SGLANG_BCG_DEBUG_INPUTS=1 dumps verify graph inputs.

Verified (run J): probe 171 tokens, 3-needle verify 7/7, C1/C3 512-token bench
complete in graph mode, no fault, no OOB, accept rate 0.66 (C1) / 0.63 (C3).

Amp-Thread-ID: https://ampcode.com/threads/T-01a0c10b-a5f8-77fc-b238-7147d12ccf29
Co-authored-by: Amp <amp@ampcode.com>
